<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	27.02	    -206	    26.96     27.15</p>
<p>91-Day	26.06	    -164	    25.90     26.19</p>
<p>182-Day     25.81	    -128	    25.69     25.92</p>
<p>364-Day     25.46				25.23     25.70</p>
<p>Last week the 343-day paper was assigned at 26.50 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   3.85 bln pesos     4.28</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   3.30 bln pesos     3.67</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   3.55 bln pesos     3.94</p>
<p>364-Day     600 million pesos   2.12 bln pesos     3.53</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.88 compared with 4.70 the week before, on demand of 15.51 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			  13  basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			  13  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			 11  basis points</p>
<p>    364-Day			 24  basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
